# Toronto Rising — walled workspace roots

This Cursor window may include extra multi-root folders that are **not** the code repo. Treat them as human browse roots unless the author explicitly asks you to use them.

## Roots

| Workspace name | Role | Default agent policy |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `toronto-rising-tts` | Code repo | Normal — primary working root |
| `Toronto Rising (Project)` | Chronicle materials (art, sheets, notes, backups, …) | **Do not** Glob / Grep / Read / Write / Delete unless the author explicitly points here |
| `TTS (Documents)` | TTS Documents tree (`Mods`, `DLC`, …) | **Do not** browse broadly. **Allowed gap:** `Saves/` (especially `TS_Save_*.json`) when save inspection or tooling diagnosis needs it |

## Tooling vs IDE walls

- Node/tts-assets scripts use **absolute paths** from `tts-assets.config.json` (`savesDir`, `backupDir`). IDE `.cursorignore` / `search.exclude` / `files.watcherExclude` do **not** block those scripts.
- `backupDir` may live under the Project root (`!! Backup Saves`); still do not crawl the Project tree unless asked.
- Walls live **in those folders** (outside git): `.cursorignore` + `.vscode/settings.json`. Repo tracks this policy via the `.code-workspace` names and this rule.

## When the author asks

If they `@`-mention a path or explicitly request a file under a walled root, you may open that path. Do not expand into a full-tree exploration afterward.